  "Aqua Roma": "W38 users 4,807 (-35.3% YoY) with 183 GA4 bookings (-68.3% YoY); conversion rate 3.8% vs 7.8% LY. Google delivered 29 bookings at $22 CPA; Meta 59 at $32. Google modelled store visits for this week are still accruing, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Aqua Kyoto": "W38 users 1,053 with 31 GA4 bookings; conversion rate 2.9%, its best of the four weeks. New in 2026, so there is no like-for-like last year. Google delivered 29 bookings at $22 CPA; Meta 59 at $32. Google modelled store visits for this week are still accruing, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Hutong NYC": "W38 users 2,946 (+6.0% YoY) with 150 GA4 bookings, up 30.4% week on week; conversion rate 5.1%. There is no last-year booking comparison: the site's SevenRooms tracking stopped on 22 September 2025 and did not resume until 15 October, so the last-year GA4, Meta and Google booking points are shown as gaps. Google delivered 24 bookings at $42 CPA; Meta 10 at $105. Google modelled store visits for this week are still accruing, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure.",
  "Hutong Miami": "W38 users 1,517 (-43.8% YoY) with 55 GA4 bookings (-55.6% YoY); conversion rate 3.6% vs 4.6% LY. Google delivered 9 bookings at $58 CPA; Meta 28 at $54. Google modelled store visits for this week are still accruing, so the latest point on the walk-in panel understates the true figure."
